# Only SLACK_ALLOWED_CHANNELS is required here.
#
# Credentials (token + "d" cookie) are normally obtained automatically by
# `slack-readonly-login`, which opens a browser and saves them to
# ~/.local/state/slack-readonly-mcp/credentials.json. Set them below only if you
# prefer to provide them manually (env overrides the saved file).

# Required. Comma-separated channel ids and/or #names. Fail-closed.
# Example: C01234567,#general,#dev-team
SLACK_ALLOWED_CHANNELS=

# Optional: provide credentials manually instead of using slack-readonly-login.
# SLACK_XOXC_TOKEN=
# SLACK_XOXD_COOKIE=

# Optional. Defaults to https://slack.com/api
# SLACK_BASE_URL=https://your-workspace.slack.com/api

# Optional. Use a system browser instead of Playwright's bundled Chromium.
# Only set this if that browser can write a profile under ~/.local/state.
# SLACK_CHROMIUM_PATH=/usr/bin/google-chrome
